# Navigation Migration Phase 3 — COMPLETE (2026-07-30)

> History: an earlier revision claimed completion prematurely; the 2026-07-26
> audit found 15 legacy links remaining (MASTER_TODO PR-28/PR-41). Those were
> actually migrated on 2026-07-30 as part of the full-stack audit fix pass.
> Verify anytime with `rg "NavigationLink\(destination:" Fit33/` — expect zero
> matches outside comments.

## What was migrated on 2026-07-30 (PR-28)

- `Fit33/SettingsView.swift` — new `SettingsRoute` enum (11 cases:
  privacySettings, blockedUsers, healthDataSync, cloudBackup, dataDownload,
  stravaSettings, fitbitSettings, healthKitSettings, termsConditions,
  privacyPolicy, notificationSettings) + `.navigationDestination(for:)`.
  DevMenu's deprecated `isActive:` link became
  `.navigationDestination(isPresented: $showDevMenu)`.
- `Fit33/ProfileView.swift` — `ProfileRoute` gained `progressPhotoGallery` and
  `olympianPath` cases; the `showWorkoutHistory` / `showFriendsList` /
  `showReceivedWorkouts` `isActive:` bindings became
  `.navigationDestination(isPresented:)` modifiers.

## Route enums that exist

`SettingsRoute` (SettingsView.swift), `DashboardRoute` (DashboardView.swift),
`ProfileRoute`, `ProgressRoute`, `PersonalizedProgramRoute`, `DevMenuRoute`,
`InBodyRoute`, `UnitSettingsRoute`, and the `CloudScheduleDayRoute` /
`ProgramScheduleDayRoute` / `ProgramScheduleWorkoutRoute` /
`ProgramScheduleExerciseRoute` structs.

Hashable conformances added for navigation values: WorkoutProgram,
SmartProgramTemplate, SmartActiveProgram, SmartProgramDay, ActiveChallenge,
ActiveGroupChallenge, CardioWorkoutDTO (all hash by `id`).

## Key Pattern: DashboardView

DashboardView's navigation destinations were extracted into a
`DashboardNavigationDestinations` ViewModifier to prevent Swift type-checker
timeout on the large body.

## Rule for new code

Never add a new `NavigationLink(destination:)` or `isActive:` link — always
use value-based navigation with a route enum + `.navigationDestination(for:)`.
